# Allow-list: the image gets only what the app needs at run time (see the
# Dockerfile). Everything else (archive, docs, experiments, slides, the
# offline question pipeline) stays out, which keeps the build context small.
*
!Requirements_Global.txt
!docker/
!resume_classifier/
!rag_system/rag_tester/question_bank/
!main_cap/cap/

# Inside the allowed folders, leave out:
# runtime data (database, uploads, secret key) -- never baked into an image
main_cap/cap/instance
# the trained evaluator weights (735 MB): mounted by docker-compose.yml instead
**/*.pt
# tests and their fixtures
main_cap/cap/test_*
main_cap/cap/resume_engine/tests
# caches and local logs
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
main_cap/cap/hybrid_diagnostics.jsonl
main_cap/cap/*.log
main_cap/cap/*_log*.txt
